[95/545] rejected; issues=["The corrected rationale still effectively communicates that the comment merits the highest actionability level (score 5) through phrasing like 'the highest actionability level' and 'meets the criteria for'—even though it avoids stating a numeric score, this language leaks the gold label by descriptor.", "The original rationale contained a specific score mapping ('This matches the description for score 3.'); the correction replaces it with 'This satisfies the rubric's description of an explicit action with concrete details on how to implement it,' which, combined with the change log entry stating 'it actually meets the criteria for the highest actionability level,' constitutes stating the gold label indirectly.", "The change log entry explicitly references 'the highest actionability level,' which is a direct statement of the gold label."]
