[173/545] rejected; issues=["The corrected rationale avoids stating a numeric score directly, which is good, but the change_log's corrected sentences themselves implicitly map to a specific rubric level by saying 'matching the rubric level that describes exactly this combination'—this is borderline but acceptable since no number is stated. More critically, the corrected rationale and change_log still contain subtle mappings to a specific rubric level. However, the main issue is that the corrected rationale is coherent and addresses all three error targets appropriately.", "On re-review, the corrected rationale corrects all three error targets: (1) it notes naming the acronym alone doesn't satisfy grounding, (2) it acknowledges authors cannot confidently determine the location, and (3) it maps the evidence to the correct rubric description without stating a numeric score. The change_log faithfully documents these corrections. The rationale is coherent and can be inserted for rescoring."]
