[253/545] rejected; issues=["The corrected rationale describes the result as 'the middle level of the rubric, where the action is explicitly stated but vague on how to execute it,' which, while not naming a numeric score, essentially encodes the score-3 description from the rubric. This is borderline direct mapping but acceptable as description rather than numeric label.", "More importantly, the corrected rationale preserves the original framing well and corrects all three error targets appropriately: (1) it removes the false claim of 'clear direction on how to implement,' (2) it removes the incorrect characterization of the solution as 'concrete,' and (3) it corrects the score mapping to the appropriate rubric level without stating a numeric score.", "Wait—re-examining: the corrected rationale does say 'meets the criteria for the middle level of the rubric, where the action is explicitly stated but vague on how to execute it.' This is a description of rubric level 3 from the task criteria. While it doesn't use the number '3,' it essentially paraphrases the rubric score definition. However, the instructions say descriptions of rubric-relevant qualities are necessary and must not be treated as leakage, so this should be acceptable.", 'All three error targets are properly addressed, the reasoning is coherent, and unrelated correct reasoning is preserved.']
