[325/545] rejected; issues=["The corrected rationale directly states the gold label/rubric level by saying the comment 'matches the highest rubric level' and gives 'all information needed,' which effectively communicates the final score/label rather than just describing rubric-relevant qualities.", "The corrected rationale overreaches on concrete details: it claims authors know 'how to carry out the experiment' and that the comment 'concretely identifies the relevant models,' but the evaluated answer only names 'pretrained ViT models' generally without specifying exact models, protocols, datasets, or metrics. The correction guidance states the threshold is high for requiring such details, but the rationale still asserts full implementation clarity that isn't fully supported by the evaluated text.", "The change_log reasons ('which matches the highest rubric level rather than a level where execution remains vague') explicitly reference rubric level assignment, which constitutes stating the gold label."]
