[366/545] rejected; issues=["The final sentence 'Overall, the comment exhibits weak grounding combined with a clearly specified content request, and no specific table, figure, or unique aspect of the paper is explicitly referenced' closely paraphrases the score-3 rubric tier ('The authors cannot confidently determine which part the comment addresses. However, the comment clearly specifies what needs to be addressed in this part.'). This effectively leaks the gold score/label mapping through semantics, violating the requirement to not directly state or closely imply a numeric final score or gold label.", "The revised second change rewrites a sentence to say 'the authors would need to make an educated guess about which part is being addressed,' which directly mirrors the score-2/3 rubric language ('the author can make an educated guess but cannot precisely identify the referenced part'). This semantic linkage to the rubric tier should be avoided in the rationale itself."]
